// Whole-measure cue regions: a cue { } that OWNS its measure — alone, and as either
// block of a voice { } { } span. Before 2026-08-05 the two per-voice flatten walks
// (GatherVoiceMusicNodes / CollectMeasuresFromNode) hand-rolled their container skip
// list and both copies were missing the cue test, so a span's cue body was walked
// twice — once as the region (cue-sized) and once flattened (full size):
//   * cue in the FIRST block:  the duplicate 4/4 rolled an extra bar — this book
//     laid out as 6 bars (`lysc layout`), while `lysc ly` exports 5. No warning.
//   * cue in a SECOND block:   the bar count held, but the duplicate silently
//     OVERLAID the sub-voice's empty placeholder in the NEXT measure (a full-size
//     aes + rests drawn on top of the closing c d e f).
// Refutation values (old spelling): 6 bars; bar 3's cue head drawn twice (once at
// cue size, once full). Fixed: 5 bars, every cue head drawn once, cue-sized.
// Guarded more directly by CueRegionTests.WholeMeasureCue* (bar counts + walked-once).
//
// ⚠️ KNOWN GAP this snapshot currently pins: rests INSIDE a cue draw full size.
// LilyPond scales them with the region (MEASURED 2026-08-05: the `lysc ly` twin of the
// solo bar renders flat+head+3 rests all at scale 0.0025 vs 0.0040 full — magstep(-4)).
// RestItem has no IsCue. When that gap is closed this snapshot moves — by design.
// LILYPOND-REF: ly/engraver-init.ly CueVoice — fontSize = #-4 (a CONTEXT property:
// it scales everything the region prints, rests included).

title "Cue Region Measure"
time 4/4
key c major

part melody

phrase test {
  c4 d e f |
  cue { aes4 r r r } |
  voice { cue { aes4 r r r } } { g4 r r r } |
  voice { g4 r r r } { cue { aes4 r r r } } |
  c4 d e f |
}

section Main {
  melody { test }
}

form main { Main }

score main "cue-region-measure" {
  staff treble melody
}
